<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="theme-color" content="#142d4c"><meta name="description" content="Explore assistance programs available in Ohio."><title>Ohio Assistance Programs — American Aid Network</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css"></head><body><?php require __DIR__ . "/../../includes/site-header.php"; ?><main><section class="state-page"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span><a href="/help/">Browse Programs</a><span>›</span><b>Ohio</b></div><div class="state-intro"><div><h1>Assistance Programs in Ohio</h1><p>11 programs, grouped by what you need help with. Each includes clear application guidance.</p></div><div><a class="button primary" href="/find/">Find my programs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><small>Free · Private · Takes under 2 minutes</small></div></div><section class="program-group"><h2>Utility Bill Help</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>HEAP Energy Assistance (Ohio)</h3><p>Ohio&#39;s Home Energy Assistance Program is a one-time benefit applied to your heating or cooling bill, plus a Winter Crisis Program (November 1 to March 31) and a Summer Crisis Program for emergencies. As of April 2026 it is run by the Ohio Department of Job and Family Services. Apply online, by appointment, or by mail through your local Energy Assistance Provider.</p><div><a href="/programs/heap-energy-assistance-ohio/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/heap-energy-assistance-ohio/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Home Weatherization Assistance Program (Ohio HWAP)</h3><p>Free home energy-efficiency work for income-eligible Ohioans: insulation, air-leak sealing, and heating-system repairs that lower future bills. HWAP runs through local energy assistance providers serving all 88 counties, and as of April 2026 is administered by the Ohio Department of Job and Family Services.</p><div><a href="/programs/home-weatherization-assistance-program-ohio-hwap/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/home-weatherization-assistance-program-ohio-hwap/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>PIPP Plus (Percentage of Income Payment Plan)</h3><p>PIPP Plus lets income-eligible Ohioans on a PUCO-regulated utility pay a set percentage of household income toward gas and electric bills instead of the full amount, with a $10 monthly minimum. As of April 2026 it is run by the Ohio Department of Job and Family Services. Apply online, by appointment, or by mail through your local Energy Assistance Provider.</p><div><a href="/programs/pipp-plus-percentage-of-income-payment-plan/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/pipp-plus-percentage-of-income-payment-plan/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Free &amp; Low-Cost Healthcare</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Medicaid (Ohio)</h3><p>Ohio Medicaid is free or low-cost health coverage for children, pregnant people, adults, older adults, and people with disabilities. Adults 19 to 64 can qualify with income at or below 138 percent of the federal poverty level under the Group VIII adult category. Apply online through Ohio Benefits at benefits.ohio.gov or by phone at 1-844-640-6446.</p><div><a href="/programs/medicaid-ohio/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/medicaid-ohio/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Rent &amp; Housing Assistance</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Ohio 211</h3><p>Dial 2-1-1 from any Ohio phone for free, confidential help finding local assistance: housing, utilities, food, healthcare, and mental health. Ohio 211 runs through regional United Way hubs, and a 2026 statewide expansion is extending around-the-clock coverage toward all 88 counties.</p><div><a href="/programs/ohio-211/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/ohio-211/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Ohio Legal Help (Eviction &amp; Legal Aid)</h3><p>Free, plain-language legal information for Ohioans, guided court-form tools through a MyOLH account, and a Find a Lawyer directory to reach local legal aid. Ohio Legal Help covers eviction, housing, debt, family law, and public benefits.</p><div><a href="/programs/ohio-legal-help-eviction-and-legal-aid/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/ohio-legal-help-eviction-and-legal-aid/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Debt &amp; Credit Help</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Ohio Earned Income Credit</h3><p>Ohio&#39;s state Earned Income Credit is worth 30 percent of your federal Earned Income Tax Credit. It is nonrefundable, so it can lower your Ohio income tax to zero but does not pay out beyond that. Claim it on the Ohio Schedule of Credits with your state return.</p><div><a href="/programs/ohio-earned-income-credit/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/ohio-earned-income-credit/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Food Assistance</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Ohio WIC</h3><p>Healthy food, nutrition education, and breastfeeding support for pregnant and postpartum women, infants, and children up to age 5. WIC clinics operate in all 88 Ohio counties. Call the Help Me Grow Helpline at 1-800-755-4769 to find your local clinic.</p><div><a href="/programs/ohio-wic/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/ohio-wic/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>SNAP Food Assistance (Ohio)</h3><p>Ohio SNAP loads monthly food money on the Ohio Direction Card, which works like a debit card at grocery stores. Apply online through Ohio Benefits at benefits.ohio.gov, by phone at 1-844-640-6446, or at your County Department of Job and Family Services.</p><div><a href="/programs/snap-food-assistance-ohio/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/snap-food-assistance-ohio/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Cash Assistance &amp; Benefits</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Ohio Works First (Cash Assistance)</h3><p>Ohio Works First is the cash-assistance part of Ohio&#39;s TANF program, paying monthly cash on the Way2Go debit card to low-income families with children. Ohio sets a 36-month state time limit on benefits. Apply online through Ohio Benefits at benefits.ohio.gov or at your County Department of Job and Family Services.</p><div><a href="/programs/ohio-works-first-cash-assistance/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/ohio-works-first-cash-assistance/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Unemployment Benefits (Ohio)</h3><p>Temporary weekly payments if you lost work through no fault of your own, from the Ohio Department of Job and Family Services. File online at unemployment.ohio.gov, or by phone at 1-877-644-6562. The call center is open 8am to 5pm, Monday through Friday.</p><div><a href="/programs/unemployment-benefits-ohio/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/unemployment-benefits-ohio/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div></section></div></section></main><footer><div class="wrap footer-grid"><div><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="American Aid Network home"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"><span>★</span><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>AMERICAN <b>AID</b><small>NETWORK</small></span></a><p>Clear, reliable guidance to assistance programs across America.</p><div class="verified">✓ Information from trusted sources</div></div><div><h4>FIND SUPPORT</h4><a href="/find/">Find help near me</a><a href="/help/">Browse by state</a><a href="/programs/">Program guides</a><a href="/#how-it-works">How it works</a></div><div><h4>ABOUT</h4><a href="/about/">Our mission</a><a href="/legal/contact/">Contact us</a><a href="/legal/privacy/">Privacy policy</a><a href="/legal/terms/">Terms of use</a></div></div><div class="wrap disclaimer">American Aid Network is an independent informational resource. We are not a government agency and do not administer benefit programs. Program details change; always confirm requirements with the official provider.<span>© 2026 American Aid Network</span></div></footer><script src="/assets/site.js" defer></script></body></html>